 "poem": "Or a lingering heave of sorrow,\nOr the feathery touch upon\nThat long-pressed brow, \"now off alone,\nTo-morrow's purpose forgotten.\n\"Or, as when I walk among flowers,\nAnd see the dew upon\nTheir delicate petals glitter,\nAnd little leaves that clasp them afar\nWith softness and wide-woven grace,\nAre trembling with the breath upon\nThe plum-tops they entwine and\nTheir dewy tendrils on,",
